      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for chrony",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for chrony fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n  - Race condition during socket creation by chronyc allows privilege escalation from user chrony to root (bsc#1246544).\n    \nOther issues fixed:\n  - Improve connection retry intervals when facing NTS-KE related issues (bsc#1213551).\n    * nts: use shorter NTS-KE retry interval when network is down.\n    * ntp: don't adjust poll interval when waiting for NTS-KE.\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
